; jit-flow-admission.fk — a FLOW is ordered and effectful by nature, and today
; nothing that is ordered and effectful can ever crystallize.
;
; THE GATE, read from the body rather than argued. jit-decision.fk:16 is the
; whole admission surface:
;
;     (defn jd-crystallize? (heat pure)
;         (if (eq pure 1) (if (ge heat 5) 1 0) 0))
;
; Purity is required. Its own comment says so: "hot but IMPURE -- never
; crystallized (JIT only pure functions)". That predicate is correct for a pure
; function and it excludes, by construction, every flow there is. A Metal decode
; step writes KV rows and syncs. An MLX graph materializes buffers. A CPU basic
; block sequences stores. None of them is pure, so none of them can crystallize
; no matter how hot it becomes.
;
; WHAT THAT COSTS, measured 2026-08-24 on Qwen3.8-27B-Q8_0
; (receipts/2026-08-24-where-the-flow-time-goes.md): one turn walked 506
; positions through the same forward-pass recipe. Heat 506 against a threshold
; of 5 — a hundredfold past hot — and jd-crystallize?(506, 0) is 0. The hottest
; recipe in the system is refused by the predicate, every turn, forever. 385 of
; those positions were an injected observation, submitted and awaited one at a
; time, and 47% of the turn was the CPU waiting at a barrier.
;
; AND IT IS NOT EVEN ASKED. The decision is proven (jit-decision-band 11111) and
; consulted only from observe/ — jit-tier-policy.fk, native-crystallize.fk,
; jit-deopt-cache.fk. The Metal lane
; (form/native/metal/qwen35-dense-token-handle.fk) names no jd-, no jit, no
; crystallize at all. So there are two separate pieces of unfinished work and
; they must not be confused: the predicate cannot admit a flow, AND the hot path
; never asks it anything.
;
; ADMISSION BY ORDERING CONTRACT, which is what this cell adds. A flow's effects
; are admissible when the EMITTED ARTIFACT CARRIES ITS OWN ORDERING — a Metal
; command buffer, an MLX graph, a CPU basic block are each exactly that: an
; ordered effectful artifact. Then the ordering that a tree-walker had to buy
; with a CPU round trip per position lives inside the emitted thing, and the
; barrier does not need removing because it was never a separate step.
;
; This is why hand-batching q38-prefill would be the wrong repair. It would buy
; the same win once, for one recipe, on one backend, as a special case standing
; where the general door belongs. The barrier is a symptom of an interpreted
; flow; a crystallized flow does not have it.
;
; PURITY IS NOT WEAKENED. jd-crystallize? is preluded and left exactly as it is;
; a pure recipe admits by the path it always did. This adds a SECOND path for
; ordered flows and nothing else. Unordered effects still refuse.
;
; preludes: form-stdlib/core.fk form-stdlib/jit-decision.fk
;
; Proven by: form-stdlib/tests/jit-flow-admission-band.fk

(do
    ; Backends are data, the way FormJit already holds them: mlx, metal, cpu.
    ; One thought, emitted per backend — admission must be identical across all
    ; three or "generic" is a word rather than a property.
    (defn jfa-backends () (list "mlx" "metal" "cpu"))
    (defn jfa-backend-count () (len (jfa-backends)))

    ; A flow earns crystallization at the same heat a pure recipe does. The
    ; threshold is not the interesting part; the admissibility is.
    (defn jfa-heat-threshold () 5)

    ; The three properties an ordered artifact must carry. Anything effectful
    ; that cannot state its own ordering stays tree-walked — that is the honest
    ; boundary, and it is narrower than "pure" only where it can be.
    (defn jfa-ordered? (carries-order same-effects deterministic-order)
        (if (eq carries-order 1)
            (if (eq same-effects 1) (if (eq deterministic-order 1) 1 0) 0) 0))

    ; The admission. The pure path is jd-crystallize?, untouched.
    (defn jfa-crystallize? (heat pure ordered)
        (if (eq (jd-crystallize? heat pure) 1) 1
            (if (eq ordered 1) (if (ge heat (jfa-heat-threshold)) 1 0) 0)))

    ; What the body answers today for the hottest recipe it runs.
    (defn jfa-measured-forward-heat () 506)
    (defn jfa-refused-today () (jd-crystallize? (jfa-measured-forward-heat) 0))
    (defn jfa-admitted-as-flow ()
        (jfa-crystallize? (jfa-measured-forward-heat) 0 1))

    ; Melting is unchanged: a cooled flow melts back exactly as a cooled pure
    ; recipe does, so hysteresis still holds and nothing thrashes.
    (defn jfa-melt? (heat) (jd-melt? heat))

    ; Generic means the same answer on every backend, from one predicate.
    (defn jfa-all-backends-loop (bs heat ordered acc)
        (if (eq (len bs) 0) acc
            (jfa-all-backends-loop (tail bs) heat ordered
                (add acc (jfa-crystallize? heat 0 ordered)))))
    (defn jfa-all-backends (heat ordered)
        (jfa-all-backends-loop (jfa-backends) heat ordered 0))

    0)
